From: ISS Android Daedalus Fork
Subject: [PATCH] wsi/x11: use coherent direct frame delivery with MIT-SHM present

The local FEXDroid direct-present extension was only used when X11 MIT-SHM
was unavailable. When the X server advertised MIT-SHM, the WSI backend
selected x11_present_to_x11_dri3() instead, even with FEXDROID_PRESENT.
The Android bridge then periodically scanned Xvfb's mutable framebuffer,
potentially capturing rows from different guest frames (horizontal tearing).

Use the completed software-present copy sent through the fxpresent slots
whenever the app has enabled that path, regardless of whether the X server
also supports MIT-SHM. Without fxpresent, keep Mesa's existing DRI3/MIT-SHM
selection unchanged. The 0007 patch already allocates fxpresent when the
app requests it (extended by the second hunk below).

--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_x11.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_x11.c
@@ -2336,7 +2336,7 @@ x11_present_to_x11(struct x11_swapchain *chain, uint32_t image_index)
    x11_capture_trace(chain);

    VkResult result;
-   if (chain->base.wsi->sw && !chain->has_mit_shm)
+   if (chain->base.wsi->sw && (!chain->has_mit_shm || chain->fxpresent))
       result = x11_present_to_x11_sw(chain, image_index);
    else
 #ifdef HAVE_X11_DRM
@@ -3532,7 +3532,7 @@
    chain->has_mit_shm = wsi_conn->has_mit_shm;
    chain->base.sw_fence_wait_in_backend = chain->base.wsi->sw;
    /* fexdroid: frames straight to the app, when it asks for them. */
-   if (chain->base.wsi->sw && !chain->has_mit_shm && os_get_option("FEXDROID_PRESENT")) {
+   if (chain->base.wsi->sw && os_get_option("FEXDROID_PRESENT")) {
       chain->fxpresent = vk_zalloc(pAllocator, sizeof(*chain->fxpresent), 8,
                                    VK_SYSTEM_ALLOCATION_SCOPE_OBJECT);
       if (chain->fxpresent)
